<title>NORWAY: FORECAST - Norway 1997 GDP growth seen at 3.9 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Norway 1997 GDP growth seen at 3.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Norwegian Finance Ministry made the following forecasts for key economic indicator growth in percentage as part of announcing a revised 1997 budget. The figures from the original forecast for 1997 of last November are included for comparison. There is no comparison for 1998.</p>
<p>					 1997 forecast     1998 forecast</p>
<p>				     Revised     November</p>
<p> Private consumption		3.2	  3.4	  2.4</p>
<p> Public consumption		 2.0	  0.9	  1.7</p>
<p> Gross fixed capital formation  8.2	  3.8	  1.9</p>
<p> Oil investment, shipping	18.5	  1.8	  1.5</p>
<p> Enterprises, mainland	    5.1	  3.3	 -1.0</p>
<p> Housing			     11.3	 11.2	  9.5</p>
<p> Public sector			3.4	 -0.8	  4.7</p>
<p> Total domestic demand	    3.8	  2.9	  2.3</p>
<p> Exports				5.1	  6.3	  6.8</p>
<p> --crude oil and natural gas    6.8	  6.7	 10.1</p>
<p> --traditional goods		4.0	  5.2	  5.5</p>
<p> Imports				5.2	  6.4	  4.5</p>
<p> --traditional goods		4.0	  6.2	  5.1</p>
<p> GDP overall			  3.9	  3.1	  3.5</p>
<p> GDP mainland			 3.3	  2.5	  2.3</p>
<p> CPI				    2.5	  2.5	  N/A</p>
<p> Budget surplus (NOK billions) 57.3	 55.4	  N/A</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
